/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (Plagiarism refers to the use of another person's content without proper acknowledgment. Manually checking documents for plagiarism can be time-consuming and difficult, especially when multiple documents need to be compared. This project aims to provide an efficient automated solution for detecting copied words and phrases. The system focuses on word-level comparison and demonstrates how data structures and string-matching algorithms can be applied to solve a practical problem. It also emphasizes manual implementation of the algorithms instead of relying on prebuilt data structure libraries.)
